{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr43tgTmCe3JFdQsg3yp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't open any files, so this diagnosis comes from the file list and my memory of the standard NestJS boilerplate layout. The line numbers are estimates, not read from the code.\n\nThe most likely cause is a profile update that overwrites the stored photo when the request doesn't include one. A first-name-only edit has no `photo` field. If the update path treats that as \"set photo to null\", the avatar link is cleared. Re-uploading sets the link again, which matches the report."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":5082,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6823630b-d85e-4f4b-bc03-4bd8db04abcd","uuid":"c4dff385-3b63-490c-9948-504d38d7f7cc","timestamp":"2026-11-08T19:59:06.068Z","request_id":"req_011Cgr43tVYU3qUqKZ5bR7dy"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgr43tgTmCe3JFdQsg3yp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018K3htP9KMAdtP451suLZms","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"candidates":[{"file":"src/users/users.service.ts","symbol":"UsersService.update","start_line":120,"end_line":190,"explanation":"Likely cause. The update path builds the payload and resolves the photo. If the DTO has no photo (a first-name-only edit), the code probably sets photo to null or undefined instead of leaving it untouched. That overwrites the stored avatar. Only an explicit photo id or an explicit null should change the photo."},{"file":"src/users/infrastructure/persistence/relational/mappers/user.mapper.ts","symbol":"UserMapper.toPersistence","start_line":40,"end_line":75,"explanation":"On update, the repository merges the existing domain user with the partial payload and maps it back to an entity. If toPersistence sets photo to null or undefined whenever domainEntity.photo is missing, the photo column is cleared on a partial update."},{"file":"src/users/infrastructure/persistence/relational/repositories/user.repository.ts","symbol":"UsersRelationalRepository.update","start_line":100,"end_line":125,"explanation":"The partial payload is merged and saved here. If the merge or save drops the existing photo relation, or lets an undefined or null photo override it, the avatar link is lost."}],"fix":{"file":"src/users/users.service.ts","description":"In UsersService.update, only touch the photo when the DTO includes it. If photo?.id is given, load the file and set it. If photo is explicitly null, set null. If photo is undefined, delete it from the clonedPayload so the existing photo is kept. Also make UserMapper.toPersistence leave photo undefined, not null, when the domain photo is undefined."}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":5082,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6823630b-d85e-4f4b-bc03-4bd8db04abcd","uuid":"0929c876-629e-428a-bd21-c63b393442bd","timestamp":"2026-11-08T19:59:09.615Z","request_id":"req_011Cgr43tVYU3qUqKZ5bR7dy"}
